    {
      "text": "maid is not dead, but sleepeth, Matt. 9:24 (Mark 5:39; Luke 8:52). While the bridegroom tarried, they all … slept, Matt. 25:5 (25:1–13). cometh unto the disciples, and findeth them asleep, Matt. 26:40. many bodies of the saints which slept arose, Matt. 27:52. Lest coming suddenly he find you sleeping, Mark 13:36. Why sleep ye? rise and pray, Luke 22:46. Lazarus sleepeth, John 11:11. it is high time to awake out of sleep, Rom. 13:11. weak and sickly among you, and many sleep, 1 Cor. 11:30. Christ … become the firstfruits of them that slept, 1 Cor. 15:20. We shall not all sleep, but we shall all be changed, 1 Cor. 15:51. which sleep in Jesus will God bring with him, 1 Thes. 4:14. let us not sleep, as do others, 1 Thes. 5:6.",
